From: Project Arctic
Subject: services: a user's own services, as Windows 10 and 11 have them.

A service of type SERVICE_USER_OWN_PROCESS or SERVICE_USER_SHARE_PROCESS
(0x50, 0x60) is a template: each logon gets an instance of it,
<name>_<logon id>, which runs in the user's session, on the user's desktop.
Wine refused the type (ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER): Logitech G HUB makes its
agent such a service, so the agent never ran and the installer waited for
it for ever. Now the template is taken and never runs itself; this logon's
instance is made at the start of the SCM (the ones of earlier logons are
dropped) and when a template is made, and an automatic one runs then;
StartService of a template starts the instance, DeleteService takes it
along. Instances run on the user's desktop (WinSta0\Default), not the services'
window station. A service has Windows' 30 s, not Wine's 10, to reach its
dispatcher: G HUB's agent took longer (ERROR_SERVICE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT).

A program's service (outside Windows' directory) of LocalSystem runs as
SYSTEM, with a token made by NtCreateToken (S-1-5-18, Administrators,
its privileges), as in Windows; every process of Arctic ran as its one
user, and G HUB's updater starts its agent in the user's session only as
SYSTEM. The system's own services keep running as before.
---
